a, 49, and James M. Amend, 79.\nThis story was found on\nBlockShopper.com\n.\nRelated\nReal Estate\nWashington Heights property tax rates exceed US average in Q4 2025\nHomeowners in Washington Heights, a neighborhood in Chicago, paid property taxes totaling 1.4% of their home values during the fourth quarter of 2025, surpassing the national average by more than 1.6 times, BlockShopper.com reports.\nReal Estate\nWest Lawn property tax rates exceed US average in Q4 2025\nHomeowners in West Lawn, a Chicago neighborhood, paid property taxes amounting to 1.3% of their home values in the fourth quarter of 2025—over 1.5 times higher than the national average, BlockShopper.com reports.\nReal Estate\nRoseland/Pullman’s property tax rate exceeds national level in Q4 2025\nHomeowners in Chicago’s Roseland/Pullman area paid property taxes equal to 1.4% of their homes’ values during Q4 2025, surpassing the national average by more than 1.6 times, BlockShopper.com reported.\nPrevious Post\n1264 W. North Shore Ave. 3, Chicago sold by John J. Okeef (trustee) and John J. Okeefe (trust)\nNext Post\nEdith Martinez-Bihler and Eric Bihlr sell 7625 N. Eastlake Terrace 108, Chicago\nTrending\nChatham property tax burden in Q4 2025 exceeds US average by over 60%\nChicago Mayor Johnson faces criticism over hiring remarks\nChicago OEMC advises public of weekend events and safety measures for early May\nCook County Sheriff’s Office details Lightsaver program success and recent enforcement actions\nVillivalam seeks $5 million appropriation for Faith by Plate Act in Illinois Senate\nIllinois Senate considers Sims’ bill for IT and payroll system upgrades\nThe Weekly Newsletter\nSign-up for the Weekly Newsletter from Chicago City Wire.\nBy submitting your information, you agree to receive exclusive content, including special promotions, and agree to our Privacy Policy and Terms of Service. By providing your phone number and checking the box to opt in, you are consenting to receive recurring SMS/MMS messages, including automated texts, to that number from our short code. Msg & data rates may apply. Reply HELP for help, STOP to end. SMS opt-in will not be sold, rented, or shared.\nSubscribe\nScroll to top\nScroll to top\nToggle Menu Close\nNews\nBusiness\nGovernment\nReal Estate\nCrime & Courts\nSchools\nNon-profit\nSports\nArts & Entertainment\nDiscussion\nDirectory\nAbout\nContact\nStories\nTerms and Conditions\nToggle Menu Close\nSearch for:\nSearch\ndata removal request\n|\nprivacy policy\ndata removal request\n×"
